email.task:
You are a team leader at a software company. Ravi, a new developer, starts work on the ShopApp project tomorrow and needs to set up the project on his laptop. Write an email to Ravi explaining the steps, using the notes below. In your email you must use:
- at least two of should, have to and need to;
- at least one passive sentence (… is given…, … is shown…);
- be due to or be scheduled to at least once.
Follow the standard layout for an email giving instructions: From / To / Date / Subject, a greeting, It should be quite easy to …, the steps with First / Then / Next / After that / Finally, a reminder (Don't forget to … when you've finished.), then Best wishes and your name, position and department.
Write 80–100 words (do not count the From, To, Date and Subject lines).
